---
source: src/cli/insights/mod.rs
assertion: kCore insight section exposes per-memory k-core decomposition using fnx_algorithms::core_number
schema:
  structural_input: ee.insights.structural_graph.v1
  output: ee.insights.v1
contracts:
  - core_number computed from memory_links structural graph via fnx_algorithms::core_number
  - items ordered by core_number descending, then degree descending, then memoryId ascending
  - mainCoreMember is true when core_number equals max_core_number
  - interpretation field carries human-readable core membership tier
  - honest empty section returned when no structural graph data is available
  - evidence includes algorithm=core_number, graphType, snapshotVersion, nodeCount, edgeCount, filterPosture, witness
evidence:
  - KCoreInsightInput.memory_id
  - KCoreInsightInput.core_number
  - KCoreInsightInput.max_core_number
  - KCoreInsightInput.degree
  - item.rank
  - item.memoryId
  - item.coreNumber
  - item.maxCoreNumber
  - item.degree
  - item.mainCoreMember
  - item.interpretation
  - item.evidence.schema
  - item.evidence.algorithm
  - item.evidence.graphType
  - item.evidence.snapshotVersion
  - item.evidence.nodeCount
  - item.evidence.edgeCount
  - item.evidence.filterPosture
  - item.evidence.witness
verified_by:
  - cargo test --lib k_core_section_emits_structural_core_number_evidence -- --nocapture
  - cargo test --lib k_core_section -- --nocapture
